"use client";

/**
 * THE GIST ROOM'S ICONS, EXPORTED FROM THE FILE.
 *
 * Every glyph below is the real `IMAGE-SVG` node from `SQUARE 2.0`, downloaded
 * through the Figma images endpoint and inlined verbatim — not a hand-drawn
 * approximation of it. Three of them were being drawn by hand before this file
 * existed (the record ring, both microphones) and every one was subtly wrong:
 * wrong stroke weight, wrong proportions, wrong optical centre.
 *
 * They are INLINED rather than served from `public/` for the same reason
 * `design-icons.tsx` inlines its own: an `<img>` cannot take `currentColor`, so
 * a glyph in a file would need one copy per colour it is ever drawn in.
 *
 * Recoloured to `currentColor` — the file's `#7E3BEB` (the house glyph) and
 * `#FF383C` (the leave control) are `--color-spotlight` and `--color-danger`
 * exactly, so the caller supplies the token and no hex lands in the slice.
 * Figma's own filter and clip ids are namespaced per glyph, because two icons
 * on one page sharing an id is a real collision.
 *
 * DO NOT redraw any of these. Re-export from the file instead.
 */

